      "writtenOn": "2019-01-21T03:54:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the generally accepted answer is that if you pass null to a @NonNull argument you should expect an NPE thrown to your face and possibly inconsistent state. ISTM this is such a common thing that you don\u0027t even need to document it (and Kotlin makes it statically checked, too ; Java IDEs will also complain loudly if you do this).\n\nIn this case, the implementation sending ERROR_INVALID_NETWORK is also a perfectly good answer, it\u0027s actually even better for the client than NPE.",
